        <definition>void printHelp</definition>
        <argsstring>(const juce::String &amp;helpText)</argsstring>
        <name>printHelp</name>
        <param>
          <type>const <ref refid="classjuce_1_1String" kindref="compound" external="/Users/jreng/Documents/Poems/JUCE/docs/tagfile.xml">juce::String</ref> &amp;</type>
          <declname>helpText</declname>
        </param>
        <briefdescription>
<para>Renders the HELP.md text to stdout through the terminal graphics context. </para>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>The function loads the markdown and mermaid stylesheets into one style manager and parses <computeroutput>helpText</computeroutput> as markdown. The width, in cells, is the column width of the markdown style: the <computeroutput>maxLineWidth</computeroutput> metric plus the <computeroutput>margin</computeroutput> metric on both sides, rounded up. The component is laid out once at that width. The row count is the height of the viewed component. The function prepares a terminal buffer for that grid, with the row count as transit room. It paints the viewed component through a terminal graphics context. The context takes the <computeroutput>Colours</computeroutput> of the style manager. <computeroutput>buffer.writeToStream (frame, styleMarkdown)</computeroutput> then writes the frame as VT bytes to a memory stream. The function writes the stream to stdout.</para>
<para><simplesect kind="pre"><para>The JUCE GUI initialiser scope is open.</para>
</simplesect>
<parameterlist kind="param"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>helpText</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>The HELP.md text, parsed as markdown. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
</para>
        </detaileddescription>
